menu "Denon/Spotify Controller"

menu "Phase 0 spike"

config DSC_SPIKE_WIFI_SSID
    string "WiFi SSID for the Phase 0 spike"
    default ""
    help
        The spike needs a real AP so WiFi DMA contends with the LCD scanout.
        Without it the R1 numbers are optimistic and must not be trusted.
        Environment, not code -- set it here rather than editing main.c.

config DSC_SPIKE_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "WiFi password for the Phase 0 spike"
    default ""

config DSC_SPIKE_URL
    string "HTTPS URL to download repeatedly during the spike"
    default "https://www.google.com/"
    help
        Should be at least a few megabytes so the TLS session and WiFi DMA
        stay busy for the whole run. A tiny page finishes instantly and
        measures nothing.

endmenu

config DSC_FACTORY_TEST
    bool "Build factory test mode instead of the application"
    default n
    help
        Manufacturing hardware exerciser (docs/SECURITY.md §7b). Must never
        be enabled in a shipping build -- tools/check_release.py fails a
        production profile that has this set.

endmenu
